      "severity": "fix",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "i18next can't read Java MessageFormat placeholders, so the error shows raw `{0}` and `{2,choice,...}`",
      "body": "The account console translates messages with i18next (`js/apps/account-ui/src/i18n.ts:25-29`). It uses the default `{{name}}` interpolation and has no ICU plugin. Server errors are rendered by `t(key, {...params})` in `js/libs/ui-shared/src/user-profile/utils.ts:74-86`. Every sibling key in this file uses `{{0}}`, for example line 27. After this change the user sees the literal text `Attribute {0} must have at least {1} and at most {2} {2,choice,0#values|1#value|1<values}.` instead of the real values. The same regression is in `js/apps/admin-ui/maven-resources/theme/keycloak.v2/admin/messages/messages_en.properties:3138`. Fix: keep `{{0}}`/`{{1}}`/`{{2}}` in both JS bundles and use plain wording (or i18next plurals) there. The `choice` form only works in the FreeMarker/Java bundles under `themes/`.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "js/apps/admin-ui/maven-resources/theme/keycloak.v2/admin/messages/messages_en.properties",
      "line": 3138,
      "severity": "fix",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "title": "Admin UI error message loses `{{n}}` interpolation",
      "body": "Same problem as the account-console bundle. The admin console also renders this key through i18next via the shared `setUserProfileServerError` (`js/libs/ui-shared/src/user-profile/utils.ts:74-86`). `{0}` and the `{2,choice,...}` clause are not interpolated, so they reach the user as raw text. Restore `{{0}}`, `{{1}}` and `{{2}}`. Medium confidence: I did not open the admin-ui i18n config, but the key previously used `{{0}}`, the same syntax as the account console.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/account/messages/messages_lt.properties",
      "line": 101,
      "severity": "fix",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "Lithuanian bundle now contains Italian text",
      "body": "`totpStep1=Installa una delle seguenti applicazioni sul tuo cellulare:` is Italian. Lithuanian users will see an Italian sentence in the OTP setup steps. The same Italian line was added at `themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/login/messages/messages_lt.properties:71` (`loginTotpStep1`). Replace both with a Lithuanian translation, e.g. `Įdiekite vieną iš šių programėlių savo mobiliajame telefone:`, or remove the key so the English fallback applies.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "themes/src/main/resources-community/theme/base/account/messages/messages_zh_CN.properties",
      "line": 112,
      "severity": "fix",
      "topic": "bug",
      "confidence": "high",
      "title": "Simplified-Chinese bundle gets a Traditional-Chinese sentence",
      "body": "`在您的手機上安裝以下應用程式之一：` uses Traditional characters and Taiwan wording (手機, 應用程式). The neighbouring lines 113-114 are Simplified (打开应用…). Use the Simplified form, e.g. `在您的手机上安装以下应用程序之一：`.",
      "anchor": "diff"
    },
    {
      "path": "misc/theme-verifier/src/main/java/org/keycloak/themeverifier/VerifyMessageProperties.java",
